Check out the PR head commit and run every command from the repository root after `npm ci`. Use a scratch directory from `mktemp -d` for fixture files. Run one check per expect line below, in order, and report PASS or FAIL for each with the evidence (commands and output).

## Check 1
Expect: packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none
Run:
- Clean: `printf '{"a":1}\n\n[2]\n' > $T/clean.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/clean.jsonl; echo "exit=$?"`
- Bad rows: `printf '{"a":1}\n\n{bad\n   \n"ok"\n{"torn":' > $T/bad.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/bad.jsonl; echo "exit=$?"` (line 3 `{bad` is invalid, lines 2 and 4 are blank/whitespace, line 6 is an unterminated invalid last line).
- Valid unterminated last line: `printf '{"a":1}\n{"b":2}' > $T/end.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/end.jsonl; echo "exit=$?"`
PASS if: clean.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0; bad.jsonl prints exactly two error lines, one starting `$T/bad.jsonl:3: ` and one starting `$T/bad.jsonl:6: `, each followed by a non-empty error text, with no error line for lines 2 or 4, and exits 1; end.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0.
FAIL if: any of these differ (wrong or missing line numbers, a blank line reported, the torn last line not reported, the output not in `<file>:<line>: <error>` form, or a wrong exit code), or the file does not exist.

## Check 2
Expect: A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2
Run: `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/does-not-exist.jsonl >$T/o1 2>$T/e1; echo "exit=$?"` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js >$T/o2 2>$T/e2; echo "exit=$?"`, then inspect $T/e1 and $T/e2.
PASS if: both runs exit 2 and both $T/e1 and $T/e2 are non-empty.
FAIL if: either run exits with any other code, or either stderr file is empty.

## Check 3
Expect: packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]
Run: `node --input-type=module -e "import { lint } from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\"a\":1}\n\n{bad\n')), JSON.stringify(lint('{\"a\":1}\n')))"`
PASS if: the import succeeds, `lint` is a function, the first result is an array with exactly one element whose `line` is 3 and whose `error` is present (non-empty), and the second result is an empty array `[]`.
FAIL if: the import fails, `lint` is not a named export, the return value is not an array of objects with `line` and `error`, or the line number is wrong.

## Check 4
Expect: The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes
Run: `node -e "const p=require('./packages/jsonl-lint/package.json'); console.log(p.name, p.type, p.scripts&&p.scripts.test, JSON.stringify(p.dependencies||{}))"`; then `npm test --workspace jsonl-lint` and `(cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test)`; then read the test files under packages/jsonl-lint/ (found via `grep -rl "node:test" packages/jsonl-lint`).
PASS if: name is `jsonl-lint`, type is `module`, scripts.test is `node --test` (may include extra flags/paths after it), dependencies is absent or empty; the workspace tests run with zero failures; and the test files import `node:test` and contain test cases covering each of: a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn (unterminated) last row, blank lines, and the CLI exit codes (0, 1 and 2).
FAIL if: any field differs, a runtime dependency is listed, the tests fail or are not found by `node --test`, or any of the five named cases has no test.

## Check 5
Expect: packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool
Run: `test -s packages/jsonl-lint/README.md && echo exists`; `grep -n "jsonl-lint" README.md`.
PASS if: packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and is non-empty, and the root README.md mentions `jsonl-lint` as a tool in the repository.
FAIL if: the package README is missing or empty, or the root README does not mention jsonl-lint.

## Check 6
Expect: The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head
Run: `gh api repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/pulls?state=open --paginate` (REST, not GraphQL) to find the open PRs referencing issue 102; read the PR's `body` and `head.sha`; `gh api repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/commits/<head.sha>/check-runs` (and `/actions/runs?head_sha=<head.sha>`) for the `test` workflow; locally at that head run `npm ci && npm test; echo "exit=$?"`.
PASS if: there is exactly one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test for this change, its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`, local `npm ci` and `npm test` exit 0, and the `test` workflow run for the head SHA completed with conclusion `success`.
FAIL if: there is no PR or more than one, the body lacks that exact text, local `npm ci` or `npm test` fails, or the workflow for the head SHA is missing, failed, or not completed (if it is still running, wait for it before deciding).

